# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics was **already properly configured** in this project. No code changes were required.

## Current Configuration Status

### 1. Package Installation ✓
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 (latest version)
- **Location**: Already present in `package.json` dependencies
- **Status**: Up-to-date with the latest version available on npm

### 2. Analytics Component Integration ✓
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 with App Router
- **Configuration File**: `app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- **Implementation**: 
  - Import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Component placement: `<Analytics />` correctly placed inside `<body>` tag
  - **Complies with official Vercel documentation**: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### 3. Code Structure
The Analytics component is properly integrated in the root layout at `app/layout.tsx`:

```tsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="vi" className="h-full">
      <body className="min-h-full flex flex-col antialiased">
        <AuthProvider>
          <BillingProvider>{children}</BillingProvider>
        </AuthProvider>
        <Analytics />  {/* ← Properly placed before closing body tag */}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This placement ensures that the Analytics component:
- Is loaded on every page of the application
- Has access to routing information through Next.js App Router
- Tracks page views and web vitals automatically
- Is correctly positioned according to Next.js and Vercel best practices

